          "text": "Abdominal pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "36–48 hours; initially vague periumbilical discomfort, now localized to the right iliac fossa/right lower quadrant; constant ache with sharp twinges on movement or coughing. 7/10 on movement today and approximately 4/10 yesterday. Worse with walking, coughing, and speed bumps."
      }
